{"label": "Anxiety", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "i constantly overthink about interactions that i believe haven't lived up to my standards, if that makes sense; or if i think i handled them terribly and could've been more articulate/funny/factually correct/empathetic/intelligent. these interactions keep replaying in my head and inducing low intensity anxiety in me and i can't seem to shake them off, sometimes for weeks on end. and if i'm lucky and had 'messed' up the situation like my brain tells me with people i'm close to then at least i get the redeeming opportunity to relieve it by clearing it up with them, but when i do, they tell me of how they hadn't even noticed it or had completed forgotten about it and although that is greatly relieving, i can't seem to keep in mind that no one is this pedantic and not follow the usual trajectory the next time something like this happens :( and it's just worse when it comes to people i don't even know as i don't get a second chance with them. only after a really long time does the reminder of my failure stop triggering anxiety in me and is met with indifference and acceptance."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Post-mortem setiap interaksi sosial itu menguras banget, terutama kalau standar kamu ke diri sendiri tinggi. Otak kamu lagi proteksi kamu dari rasa malu — tapi cara itu sering bikin lebih capek. Kamu nggak harus sempurna di setiap percakapan."}]}
